IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgj-part5-office-name`

-- Assertions written by the independent wave-2 reader for parts sgj, sgk and sgl (a fresh agent that wrote its answers from the text before it opened any encoding),
-- kept here where the encoding was changed to agree with them. Each carries the reader's scenario number and the answer the reader expected.

-- reader scenario 151b, s 144(2) (text lines 11585-11590): an officer signs a cheque without the company's name and the company has not paid: the officer is also liable to the holder (a cheque is a negotiable instrument: limb (c) of the same subsection writes "cheque or other negotiable instrument"); expected JUST TRUE.
-- arguments: the instrument; the person signed, issued or authorised it without the company's name; the amount due has been paid by the company
#ASSERT `s 144(2) the person is liable to the holder of the instrument for the amount due on it` `s 144(2) a cheque` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- reader scenario 152, s 144(2): the same cheque, the company has paid: not liable to the holder ("unless it is paid by the company"); expected JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 144(2) the person is liable to the holder of the instrument for the amount due on it` `s 144(2) a cheque` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
